{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-9fbb21b195380114", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# Conformer: Convolution-augmented Transformer for Speech Recognition\narXiv: 2005.08100\nAuthors: Anmol Gulati, James Qin, Chung-Cheng Chiu, Niki Parmar, Yu Zhang, Jiahui Yu, Wei Han, Shibo Wang, Zhengdong Zhang, Yonghui Wu, Ruoming Pang\nYear: 2020 | Venue: \nTopic: asr\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. Proposes the Conformer architecture that organically combines convolution neural networks and transformers to model both local and global dependencies in an audio sequence in a parameter-efficient way.\n  2. Introduces a novel Conformer block featuring a multi-headed self-attention module and a convolution module sandwiched between two Macaron-style feed-forward modules with half-step residual connections.\n  3. Integrates relative sinusoidal positional encoding into the multi-headed self-attention module to improve generalization across varying input lengths.\n  4. Achieves state-of-the-art word error rates of 1.9%/3.9% on the LibriSpeech test-clean/test-other benchmarks using an external language model.\n  5. Demonstrates parameter efficiency by showing that a 30M-parameter Conformer model outperforms a 139M-parameter Transformer Transducer.\n  6. Provides comprehensive ablation studies validating the superiority of the Macaron-style feed-forward structure, depthwise convolutions, and stacking the convolution module after the self-attention module.\n\nTags: ASR\n---\n2504.02386", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "f3bfbc9c-36b6-4486-94dd-0fbea3ff4a3d", "uuid": "59302e59-ccaa-49b4-88b2-eb41ab02f1df", "timestamp": "2026-08-05T09:22:10.598Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# Conformer: Convolution-augmented Transformer for Speech Recognition\narXiv: 2005.08100\nAuthors: Anmol Gulati, James Qin, Chung-Cheng Chiu, Niki Parmar, Yu Zhang, Jiahui Yu, Wei Han, Shibo Wang, Zhengdong Zhang, Yonghui Wu, Ruoming Pang\nYear: 2020 | Venue: \nTopic: asr\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. Proposes the Conformer architecture that organically combines convolution neural networks and transformers to model both local and global dependencies in an audio sequence in a parameter-efficient way.\n  2. Introduces a novel Conformer block featuring a multi-headed self-attention module and a convolution module sandwiched between two Macaron-style feed-forward modules with half-step residual connections.\n  3. Integrates relative sinusoidal positional encoding into the multi-headed self-attention module to improve generalization across varying input lengths.\n  4. Achieves state-of-the-art word error rates of 1.9%/3.9% on the LibriSpeech test-clean/test-other benchmarks using an external language model.\n  5. Demonstrates parameter efficiency by showing that a 30M-parameter Conformer model outperforms a 139M-parameter Transformer Transducer.\n  6. Provides comprehensive ablation studies validating the superiority of the Macaron-style feed-forward structure, depthwise convolutions, and stacking the convolution module after the self-attention module.\n\nTags: ASR\n---\n2504.02386", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
